@startuml wvf-incident
skinparam dpi 150
hide empty description
title Wolverine factory: IncidentSaga (id = app + environment + generation; signals join)

[*] --> Detected : alert webhook, confirmed Unhealthy reads\n(both suppressed while the environment deploys),\nDeliveryTrain: prod deployment failed
state Detected : open or join the incident issue; notify the owner;\nhold the environment's DeliveryTrain\n(the incident's own hotfix and rollback pass the hold)
Detected --> Triaging
state Triaging : /_healthcheck, /_telemetry, App Insights errors,\nrecent releases; read-only AI analyst session
Triaging --> RollingBack : a recent release correlates, no migration\nsince the previous one, policy allows
Triaging --> Fixing : a code defect, or a migration\nmakes rollback unsafe
Triaging --> Escalated : unclear
state RollingBack : Rollback(env, previous release) to the DeliveryTrain\n(Sign-off per policy); items of the rolled-back release:\nUndelivered(env) within their settle window
state Fixing : WorkItemSaga on the hotfix plan\n(rank top, every quality gate)
RollingBack --> Verifying : deployment succeeded
Fixing --> Verifying : DeliveredTo(prod)
state Escalated : the owner decides
Escalated --> RollingBack : owner: roll back
Escalated --> Fixing : owner: fix forward
Escalated --> Verifying : owner: fixed by hand
Escalated --> Resolved : owner: close
state Verifying : Healthy reads and error rate at baseline for the window
Verifying --> Resolved : signal clear
Verifying --> Triaging : still failing
state Resolved : note from the history; close the issue;\nrelease the DeliveryTrain hold
Resolved --> [*]
Detected --> Escalated : timeout
Triaging --> Escalated : timeout
RollingBack --> Escalated : timeout or failed
Fixing --> Escalated : timeout
Verifying --> Escalated : timeout
@enduml
